# Indian Sign Language (ISL) Recognition

A deep learning project that recognises hand-sign letters from a single photo.
Project: PRAICP-1000-IndiSignLang. Everything is in one Jupyter notebook.

## Goal
1. Image preprocessing
2. A machine learning model that predicts the sign

## Dataset
- 4,971 close-up photos of one hand on a plain background (after removing 1 duplicate)
- 24 classes: letters A to Y without J and Z
- Split: 3,548 train / 713 validation / 710 test

The dataset is not included in this repository.

## What the notebook does
- Checks the data for corrupted files and duplicates
- Preprocesses images (padded resize to 160x160, augmentation, class weights)
- Trains three models: a baseline CNN, MobileNetV2 and EfficientNetB0, plus an ensemble
- Evaluates with accuracy, macro-F1, confusion matrix and Grad-CAM
- Tests robustness on dark, blurred and noisy images
- Saves the model and includes a live webcam demo

## Results (test set)
| Model | Accuracy |
|---|---|
| Baseline CNN | 99.72% |
| EfficientNetB0 | 99.15% |
| MobileNetV2 | 94.23% |
| Ensemble | 99.86% |

Note: the baseline CNN dropped to 6.6% accuracy on darkened images, so the final
notebook uses stronger augmentation and picks the model by robustness.

## How to run
1. Open `PRAICP_1000_IndiSignLang_Advanced_v2.ipynb` in Google Colab with a GPU.
2. Upload the dataset zip and unzip it to `/content/isl_data`.
3. Run all cells from the top.

## Limitations
Only 24 static one-handed letters. No J, Z, words or sentences.
Works best with close-up photos on a plain background.

## Tech
Python, TensorFlow/Keras, scikit-learn, OpenCV
